title A wall that reads the index
prompt the baton -- take the next agent-doable lap, reds first
think The open read stash@{0} before anything else, per the dead-lap clause: eight files, stamped 20260907.135743, a finished lap the round-open parked with no session log written. Reading its diff against its own base showed REDS %524 closed by taking the class rather than the instance.
think The cold roster ran first on the clean tree, 173 guards over 1,528s: readme_reach red, reds_fold red, standing_equipment red -- three rows, one root. construction/ITINERARY.md linked archive/REDS-a-label-is-not-its-target-rows-571.md while that shelf stands at rows-570, a peer's fold planned one number and upstream landed another. That is %524's fourth firing, live, on the card I was about to edit.
think So the recovery and the red were the same lap. git stash pop restored the work; both witnesses were then run on metal rather than trusted from the diff.
obs The mechanism, plainly: tools/fixtures/r/readme_reach_scan.sh gained one option, --store worktree|index. The index store reads document bodies through one long-lived git cat-file --batch and tests link targets against the git ls-files path set plus its directory prefixes. tools/hooks/pre-commit gained rule six, which calls that scan with --store index and refuses the commit on verdict=living_link_broken.
obs The index rather than a staged set is the whole finding. All four firings of %524 arrived by rebase, so no staged-set trigger could ever have seen one -- the break is authored nowhere and lands everywhere. Rule six therefore carries no trigger of its own, which is affordable because the crawl costs 544ms against rule one's ten-second render.
obs One scan, two stores, rather than a second reader: writing the commit-time question its own crawl would put one rule in two files, which is %382 exactly.
obs The water row read as the lap's own argument. The happy zone is where a wrong value tastes wrong immediately; this reading had been sitting in the thin edge of a cold pass that runs half an hour after the push. Rule six moves it inside.
obs What the recovery cost, and it is worth saying: the parked lap left no log, so the only account of why those eight files were edited was the card. A stash record names files and a stamp; it cannot name a reason.
loom witness=readme_reach_witness cases=15 broken_in_living=0 broken_in_testimony=1227
loom witness=generated_page_freshness_witness cases=16 link_wall_bitten=yes link_wall_free=yes
loom roster=cold guards=173 green=167 red=3 gated=3 wall_s=1528
rota lap 4188, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; its fixed seat named the shape of this lap's own repair, a reading moved out of the thin edge and into the happy zone where it is instant.
file tools/fixtures/r/readme_reach_scan.sh the --store option; the index store and its path-prefix existence test
file tools/hooks/pre-commit rule six, the link wall, refusing rather than regenerating
